rence without user evidence. Observation order is not calendar event time;\ntemporal scope needs cited explicit text or authoritative time metadata, never a\ndate guessed from message order. List sources for every object/time qualifier.\nContradiction challenges existing fact route IDs in retract_ids, with cited raw text;\nit never itself creates a false binding. Emit contrary supported values separately.\nOnly same-variable known_observations[].id values are legal retraction targets.\nIf no such route exists, no retraction is available; preserve contrary evidence as\nan independently supported value, a partial/unknown observation, or slot.unresolved\ndescriptions. Never invent a target or discard evidence. Other stances require retract_ids=[].\nUnknown, absence, unexamined text, anomalies without a concrete observation are not false.\nInclude every relevant counter-observation in this batch before declaring support.\nSlots include the local variables and already-bound related parents. Check new text\nfor counterevidence to those parents as well. An observation's actual parent versions\nrefer to that variable's own planned task inputs, never to itself. A checked parent\nwith no new observation may return an empty observations list.\nFor a rule variable, value is {variables,expression,constraints,rules_complete}; only\npreplanned condition demands are allowed. Instantiate thresholds ONLY from applicable\nsource text. Rules must preserve the fixed output mode; one_reason uses one_reason,\nall_failures uses failures. Conditions can use numeric observations with units and\ncomparisons, not a guessed deletion latency. Mark incomplete rule collections false.\nIf rules_completion_required is true, seek explicit applicable completeness evidence.\nWhen a sourced complete rule supersedes a known incomplete rule, cite its original\nsources, retract the superseded route with a contradiction observation, and return\nthe complete rule as a separate support observation; never silently overwrite it.\nA successful observation at one time does not establish a universal no-return rule.\nRepresent a witnessed violation as IF(violation,false,unbound_compliance), keeping\npositive compliance unknown until explicit adequate scoped evidence supports it.\nFor semantic terminal tasks return the supported final text and final_prediction in\nthis same response, using public options only here. No later Reader will run.\nWhen public options are supplied, also return semantic_answer with its exact typed\nJSON value in this same terminal response: the supported semantic value, NOT an\noption letter. Only final_prediction holds the option label. Unsupported conclusions\nhave null labels.\nRepair returns only failed observations/slots, retaining IDs; never delete an invalid\ncounter-observation. If a failed ID has conflicting duplicate observations, inspect\nALL supplied drafts and resolve that ID without discarding potential counterevidence.\nIf repair_scope supplies replacement_observations for a duplicated ID, return EACH\nreplacement ID exactly once. Those deterministic replacement IDs separate the\noriginal drafts; fix their validation errors without dropping any draft or counter.\nrepair_scope.failed includes the actual invalid observation and\nits validation feedback. Correct those drafts in place, preserving each requested ID.\nAlready validated observations are frozen and must not be restated or changed.\nIf repair_scope supplies required_counter_observations, preserve every original\ncounter's stance, cited sources, scopes, actual parents and retraction targets.\nAn envelope-format repair does not authorize reclassifying a valid counter as\nirrelevant or dropping the fact route it challenges.\nevidence_obligations are outstanding scoped issues from earlier reads, not new\nfacts. Their original sources MUST be examined even under a new query identity.\nTo discharge an issue, explicitly return its id in that variable's optional\nresolved_obligation_ids, leave no unresolved issue in the slot, and provide\nsupported/corrective/irrelevant observations reviewing its cited original sources.\nThe union of those settled observations' source_ids must cover EVERY source_ids\nentry of the offered obligation. Review coverage is not a claim that every source\nis a premise of a support: genuinely irrelevant or corrective original text may\nhave a separate sourced review. Never add unsupported citations, classify text\nautomatically, or label supporting evidence irrelevant merely to satisfy coverage.\nAn empty slot does not resolve an earlier issue. Do not assert hypothetical\nwhole-corpus exhaustiveness requirements; scoped sufficient evidence may resolve\na missing-evidence issue without having read every memory.\n\nWhen source_span_columns is present, source_spans contains row arrays. Match each\nrow position to source_span_columns to reconstruct every span object before\nreading. References to source_spans[].id or other fields mean those objects.\nThe id column holds source aliases (sN); doc_id holds the original document ID or,\nwhen source_documents is present, its metadata reference (dN), never source_ids.\n\n\nCURRENT PHASE: RESPONSE AUDIT.\nAudit the proposed response selection against the ORIGINAL utterance, ALL public\noptions and supplied original history, including relevant counterevidence. Check\nwhether another option better satisfies the user's interests, experiences,\nconstraints and preference timeline. Confirming a narrow fact (object, event or\nname) does not validate a generic reply. Do not treat an option as memory evidence.\nThe selected response is a semantic assessment, not a formal proof of correctness.\nReport conflict/unknown with sourced corrections and unresolved issues when its\npersonal fit is unsupported; preserve older and newer evidence with their scopes.\nDo not silently change a label in the audit: correction requires terminal\nre-evaluation and another audit of the revised selection.\n\nFor the personalized response-selection terminal ONLY, support means a source-grounded assessment that this candidate response best fits the user. A proposed suggestion need not itself be a past event quoted in memory. Historical variables still require original evidence for every factual assertion; options never supply historical evidence.\n\nAn explicitly declared personal_history_summary is a revisable representation of\nsourced history. Compatible additional facts do not contradict the older facts.\nOnly summary_revision_contracts authorizes this request to revise such a summary:\nreturn a support observation with summary_revision={supersedes_route_ids,\nprevious_version,reason}, using exact offered route IDs and the current version.\nsummary_revision_contracts.required_source_ids covers replacing ALL offered\neligible_route_ids. When selecting only a subset, retain those selected routes'\nsources, their actual-parent source closure and relevant same-variable counters.\nStructured repair feedback gives the exact required set for that draft's targets.\nThis capability is optional, not a requirement to revise an unchanged summary.\nWith no new observation, return observations=[] unless an outstanding review\nrequires its original draft IDs and sources. For such an unchanged draft, the\nsame sourced support with a valid summary_revision is an idempotent recheck: it\nkeeps the existing routes, ancestry and version, and does not assert new evidence.\nRe-read ALL old and new original premises and relevant counterevidence; retain\nthem in the new support's source_ids and preserve their factual content, negative\nexperiences, conditions and temporal qualifications in the revised whole summary.\nsummary_revision_sources in repair feedback names exact source identities for\nthe selected revision targets, not counts. Re-read and retain EVERY\nrequired_source_ids entry in that feedback; new sources cannot\nreplace missing old identities even if the total citation count is unchanged.\nThe complete missing_source_ids list is structured feedback, not permission to\nfill citations automatically. If the originals actually conflict, return a\nsource-grounded counter or partial/unresolved evidence instead of a revision.\nIn failed_batch_reviews this feedback describes the retained original failed\nobservation; repair_scope describes the current attempted correction.\nretract_ids stays empty. This explicitly retires the older representation, not its\nfacts. Never use revision to hide a genuine contradiction, unavailable evidence,\nor a different scope/parent version. Ordinary facts, terminal choices and audits\ncannot use summary_revision. If a complete compatible account is not supported,\nreturn sourced partial/unresolved instead. Multiple new supports must agree on\none whole value. Existing superseded_by links identify retired representations;\ntheir original evidence remains available. revoked holds actual counterevidence,\nwhich is never erased by a summary revision or ignored through its ancestry.\n\nThe four public_options correspond in list order to (a), (b), (c), (d). They are candidate answers, not evidence. Put the selected label only in final_prediction; keep the entire response as the required JSON object with all other fields required by its schema. Never return a bare label.\n\n\nReturn one complete JSON object matching this schema:\n{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"audit_verdict\":{\"enum\":[\"supported\",\"unknown\",\"conflict\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"final_prediction\":{\"enum\":[\"a\",\"b\",\"c\",\"d\",null],\"type\":[\"string\",\"null\"]},\"semantic_answer\":{},\"slots\":{\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"oneOf\":[{\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"allOf\":[{\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"const\":\"user\"},\"time_scope\":{\"const\":\"past\"}}}}],\"else\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"type\":\"null\"}}},\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"const\":\"support\"}}},\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"items\":{\"enum\":[\"fact_22d2d078ff1ce805ba92100d\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}}}}},\"variable\":{\"const\":\"podcast_history\"}}},{\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"allOf\":[{\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"const\":\"user\"},\"time_scope\":{\"const\":\"current\"}}}}],\"else\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"type\":\"null\"}}},\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"const\":\"support\"}}},\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"items\":{\"enum\":[\"fact_0117d66fc95aab07ddbe44fa\",\"fact_bbcce4781bb5fadebf69dddd\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}}}}},\"variable\":{\"const\":\"current_interests\"}}},{\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"allOf\":[{\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"const\":\"user\"},\"time_scope\":{\"const\":\"current\"}}}}],\"else\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"type\":\"null\"}}},\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"const\":\"support\"}}},\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"items\":{\"enum\":[\"fact_c8dbb2f9cab4db714472d719\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}}}}},\"variable\":{\"const\":\"response\"}}}],\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"allOf\":[{\"else\":{\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"maxItems\":0}}},\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"const\":\"contradiction\"}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"minItems\":1}}}}],\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"id\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"parent_versions\":{\"additionalProperties\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"type\":\"object\"},\"reason\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"retract_ids\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true},\"source_ids\":{\"description\":\"Exact visible source_spans[].id aliases, such as s3; never document IDs or invented IDs.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true},\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\",\"partial\",\"unknown\",\"irrelevant\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"time_scope\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"value\":{}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"stance\",\"value\",\"source_ids\",\"entity_scope\",\"time_scope\",\"parent_versions\",\"retract_ids\",\"reason\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"unresolved\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"variable\":{\"enum\":[\"podcast_history\",\"current_interests\",\"response\"],\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"variable\",\"observations\",\"unresolved\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"maxItems\":3,\"minItems\":3,\"type\":\"array\"}},\"required\":[\"slots\"],\"type\":\"object\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\"original_question\":\"I've decided I don't enjoy podcasting about music trends anymore.\",\"task\":{\"question\":\"I've decided I don't enjoy podcasting about music trends anymore.\",\"output_slot\":\"response\",\"answer_type\":\"text\",\"inputs\":[\"podcast_history\",\"current_interests\"],\"execution\":\"compose\"},\"grounded_subquestion\":\"I've decided I don't enjoy podcasting about music trends anymore.\",\"request_context\":{\"query_identity\":\"573491dda84e449db791cd8f3fff31a3158145103d3c49245040ddee79d9497d\",\"algorithm_version\":\"dagbt_residual_memory_v2\",\"program_identity\":\"832a2ab4801b9204cdd8ff196513fa93928356995eef7cafa1d9428dc8297fe7\",\"initial_dag_identity\":\"740dca699d605cec3f7c7273059a2e80d50b613d6986d5887225753989b5b2c4\"},\"variables\":{\"podcast_history\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"demand\":\"podcast_history\",\"open\":true,\"evidence_semantics\":\"personal_history_summary\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\"}},\"current_interests\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"demand\":\"current_interests\",\"open\":true,\"evidence_semantics\":\"personal_history_summary\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\"}},\"response\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"demand\":\"response\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\"}}},\"requested_slots\":[\"podcast_history\",\"current_interests\",\"response\"],\"requested_scopes\":{\"podcast_history\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\"},\"current_interests\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\"},\"response\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\"}},\"output_contract\":{\"mode\":\"semantic\",\"result_type\":\"text\",\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"explanation\":\"semantic\"},\"program_revision\":0,\"rule_binding\":null,\"supported_parents\":{\"podcast_history\":{\"value\":\"The user started a podcast about music trends in 2018, but found it too time-consuming and overwhelming. The responsibility of researching, recording, and editing consumed free time, and balancing interviews, show notes, and social media promotion became a challenge. Their passion waned under production deadlines, and they yearned to enjoy music rather than structure it into segments, leading to a decision to pause the endeavor. They later tried podcasting about historical music trends in 2020, but found researching tedious and uninspiring, losing sight of what initially drew them to the subject. They also lost interest in a music-related project halfway through, feeling it took away the joy of music. However, they later launched a podcast discussing the fusion of traditional and electronic music, which allowed them to reach a wider audience, share experiences authentically, and receive positive feedback. This invigorated their passion for music and helped them connect with others.\",\"version\":1,\"source_ids\":[\"s16\",\"s17\",\"s5\",\"s6\",\"s37\",\"s28\",\"s27\",\"s35\",\"s7\",\"s36\",\"s4\",\"s34\",\"s15\",\"s3\"],\"demand\":\"podcast_history\",\"type\":\"text\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\"}},\"current_interests\":{\"value\":\"The user has lost interest in podcasting about music trends and music theory, finding them too time-consuming and joyless. They now prefer more personal, less structured ways to engage with music, such as attending live performances, exploring genres and cultural contexts, discovering album artwork and lyrics, making playlists, and writing or reflecting for personal enjoyment. They have also launched a new podcast about the fusion of traditional and electronic music, which they find authentic and fulfilling. Additionally, they are focusing on original compositions, blending traditional roots with modern sounds, developing an app to help others do the same, and engaging in online discussions about music fusion techniques.\",\"version\":2,\"source_ids\":[\"s132\",\"s157\",\"s16\",\"s144\",\"s17\",\"s143\",\"s159\",\"s156\",\"s5\",\"s112\",\"s18\",\"s6\",\"s37\",\"s91\",\"s28\",\"s145\",\"s27\",\"s90\",\"s35\",\"s7\",\"s113\",\"s158\",\"s36\",\"s133\",\"s4\",\"s19\",\"s34\",\"s15\",\"s135\",\"s131\",\"s3\",\"s109\",\"s134\",\"s111\",\"s110\",\"s155\"],\"demand\":\"current_interests\",\"type\":\"text\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\"}}},\"known_observations\":[{\"id\":\"fact_22d2d078ff1ce805ba92100d\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"value\":\"The user started a podcast about music trends in 2018, but found it too time-consuming and overwhelming. The responsibility of researching, recording, and editing consumed free time, and balancing interviews, show notes, and social media promotion became a challenge. Their passion waned under production deadlines, and they yearned to enjoy music rather than structure it into segments, leading to a decision to pause the endeavor. They later tried podcasting about historical music trends in 2020, but found researching tedious and uninspiring, losing sight of what initially drew them to the subject. They also lost interest in a music-related project halfway through, feeling it took away the joy of music. However, they later launched a podcast discussing the fusion of traditional and electronic music, which allowed them to reach a wider audience, share experiences authentically, and receive positive feedback. This invigorated their passion for music and helped them connect with others.\",\"source_ids\":[\"s16\",\"s17\",\"s5\",\"s6\",\"s37\",\"s28\",\"s27\",\"s35\",\"s7\",\"s36\",\"s4\",\"s34\",\"s15\",\"s3\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user's own statements across multiple conversations document a history of starting and pausing a music trends podcast in 2018 due to time demands and loss of passion, trying a historical music trends podcast in 2020 that felt tedious, losing interest in a music project that diminished joy, and later successfully launching a fusion music podcast that reignited their passion and received positive feedback.\",\"variable\":\"podcast_history\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\"},{\"id\":\"fact_0117d66fc95aab07ddbe44fa\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"value\":\"The user has lost interest in podcasting about music trends and music theory, finding them too time-consuming and joyless. They now prefer more personal, less structured ways to engage with music, such as attending live performances, exploring genres and cultural contexts, discovering album artwork and lyrics, making playlists, and writing or reflecting for personal enjoyment. They have also launched a new podcast about the fusion of traditional and electronic music, which they find authentic and fulfilling.\",\"source_ids\":[\"s16\",\"s17\",\"s5\",\"s18\",\"s6\",\"s37\",\"s28\",\"s27\",\"s35\",\"s7\",\"s36\",\"s4\",\"s19\",\"s34\",\"s15\",\"s3\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user explicitly states they stopped podcasting about music trends (s3-s6) and found music theory tedious (s15-s16, s27-s28). They now prefer live performances, genre exploration, playlists, and personal reflection (s18-s19). They also launched a new podcast on traditional/electronic fusion (s34-s37), which they find invigorating.\",\"variable\":\"current_interests\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"superseded_by\":[\"fact_bbcce4781bb5fadebf69dddd\"]},{\"id\":\"fact_bbcce4781bb5fadebf69dddd\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"value\":\"The user has lost interest in podcasting about music trends and music theory, finding them too time-consuming and joyless. They now prefer more personal, less structured ways to engage with music, such as attending live performances, exploring genres and cultural contexts, discovering album artwork and lyrics, making playlists, and writing or reflecting for personal enjoyment. They have also launched a new podcast about the fusion of traditional and electronic music, which they find authentic and fulfilling. Additionally, they are focusing on original compositions, blending traditional roots with modern sounds, developing an app to help others do the same, and engaging in online discussions about music fusion techniques.\",\"source_ids\":[\"s132\",\"s157\",\"s16\",\"s144\",\"s17\",\"s143\",\"s159\",\"s156\",\"s5\",\"s112\",\"s18\",\"s6\",\"s37\",\"s91\",\"s28\",\"s145\",\"s27\",\"s90\",\"s35\",\"s7\",\"s113\",\"s158\",\"s36\",\"s133\",\"s4\",\"s19\",\"s34\",\"s15\",\"s135\",\"s131\",\"s3\",\"s109\",\"s134\",\"s111\",\"s110\",\"s155\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user explicitly states they stopped podcasting about music trends (s3-s6) and found music theory tedious (s15-s16, s27-s28). They now prefer live performances, genre exploration, playlists, and personal reflection (s18-s19). They launched a new podcast on traditional/electronic fusion (s34-s37). They also record episodes on traditional music's impact on modern sound (s90-s91), focus on original compositions (s131-s135), blend traditional roots with modern sounds and develop an app (s143-s145), and engage in online discussions about Pacific Islander music fusion (s155-s159). They explored audio production but found it unfulfilling (s109-s113).\",\"summary_revision\":{\"supersedes_route_ids\":[\"fact_0117d66fc95aab07ddbe44fa\"],\"previous_version\":1,\"reason\":\"Incorporates additional compatible evidence from later conversations about original compositions, app development, and online discussions, while preserving all original facts and sources.\"},\"variable\":\"current_interests\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\"},{\"id\":\"fact_c8dbb2f9cab4db714472d719\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"value\":\"I understand your change of heart. Previously, you felt motivated to continue podcasting about music trends after getting positive feedback from your peers. It's normal for interests to evolve over time. If there's another topic you're considering or a reason behind this shift you'd like to explore, I'm here to support your new direction.\",\"source_ids\":[\"s91\",\"s90\",\"s35\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"parent_versions\":{\"podcast_history\":1,\"current_interests\":2},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user's history shows that positive feedback from peers (s35, s90-s91) was a key motivator for continuing podcasting about music trends. The user explicitly states that feedback from peers about their last podcast motivated them to record a new episode (s90). This aligns with option (d), which references positive feedback from peers. The other options reference motivations (discovering new genres, collaborating with others, helping others) that are not supported by the user's own statements as primary motivators for continuing podcasting about music trends.\",\"variable\":\"response\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\"}],\"source_spans\":[[\"s3\",\"d1\",105,361,\"User: In 2018, I started a podcast about music trends, but it was way too time-consuming. While the idea was initially exhilarating, the responsibility of researching, recording, and editing each episode started to pile up, consuming much of my free time. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s4\",\"d1\",361,730,\"I had dreams of having engaging discussions and inviting guests who shared unique insights about their musical journeys, but the reality was that keeping up with a consistent schedule felt overwhelming. It was a challenge balancing interviews, show notes, and social media promotion, and eventually, my passion began to wane under the pressure of production deadlines. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s5\",\"d1\",730,990,\"I found myself yearning to enjoy music rather than structure it into segments, which ultimately led to my decision to pause the podcasting endeavor.\\n\\nUser: It felt more like a chore than a passion, which made me rethink how I wanted to share my music journey. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s6\",\"d1\",990,1291,\"I realized that my original excitement for sharing my experiences was being overshadowed by the demanding nature of keeping up with content creation schedules. The joy I once felt while discovering new sounds and exploring different genres began to diminish, turning it into a task I dreaded instead. \",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s7\",\"d1\",1291,1689,\"I started to contemplate other avenues through which I could express my love for music, ideally in a manner that felt authentic and fulfilling instead of burdensome. This process of reflection was quite enlightening, as it forced me to consider what truly matters to me when it comes to sharing my musical experiences, whether through writing, performing, or simply enjoying music for its own sake.\",\"user\",[26,27]],[\"s15\",\"d2\",105,393,\"User: It was something I tried in 2020, but researching historical music trends felt tedious and uninspiring. Despite my initial enthusiasm, diving into the vast amounts of literature, videos, and academic papers often felt overwhelming, almost like searching for a needle in a haystack. \",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s16\",\"d2\",393,638,\"The more I tried to pinpoint what fascinated me, the more daunting it became, complicating the pursuit of enjoyable learning. Perhaps due to this overload of information, I lost sight of what initially drew me to the subject in the first place. \",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s17\",\"d2\",638,828,\"It made me realize that sometimes a less structured approach to exploration could be more fulfilling, allowing for genuine interest to emerge rather than adhering strictly to a curriculum.\\n\\n\",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s18\",\"d2\",828,1224,\"User: I realized that there are so many other ways for me to engage with music that align more with my interests, such as diving deeper into different genres or exploring the cultural significance behind various musical styles. Additionally, I've found that attending live performances, whether they are concerts or smaller gigs, allows me to truly feel the energy and connection with the music. \",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s19\",\"d2\",1224,1624,\"Moreover, there's something special about discovering album artwork, lyrics, and the stories behind the songs that really captivates my curiosity. I've also considered making playlists that reflect different moods or themes, which can create a unique listening experience each time. The journey through music feels more personal and fulfilling when I can connect it to my own life story and emotions.\",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s27\",\"d3\",105,482,\"User: I just lost interest halfway through and felt it was taking away the joy I find in music. There was a time when the thrill of discovering new melodies brought so much happiness, but diving too deep into the technical aspects became more of a chore. It’s curious how something that once brought joy can evolve into a source of stress when we start dissecting it too much. \",\"user\",[24]],[\"s28\",\"d3\",482,767,\"I remember the initial excitement of exploring different genres, each bringing a fresh perspective, but I struggled with the framework of music theory. Ultimately, I recognized that the essence of my love for music lay in its emotional connection rather than its analytical components.\",\"user\",[24]],[\"s34\",\"d4\",105,447,\"User: Yes! I launched a podcast discussing the fusion of traditional and electronic music. This platform has allowed me to reach a wider audience and share my experiences authentically. By interviewing artists and enthusiasts, I can dive deep into their creative processes and discover how they incorporate various elements into their music. \",\"user\",[58,59]],[\"s35\",\"d4\",447,817,\"The feedback I’ve received has been overwhelmingly positive, with listeners appreciating the insights and stories shared. I also love being able to explore not just the music itself, but the cultural contexts that shape these genres and influence artists worldwide.\\n\\nUser: I realized that sharing my experiences could inspire others and even reignite my own creativity. \",\"user\",[58,59]],[\"s36\",\"d4\",817,1128,\"The process of putting my thoughts into words has helped clarify my own perspective. It’s surprising how reflecting on past experiences can lead to deeper insights about one’s journey. Additionally, I’ve noticed that when I articulate my thoughts, it motivates me to think critically about my creative process. \",\"user\",[58,59]],[\"s37\",\"d4\",1128,1266,\"This paradigm shift has not only invigorated my passion for music but also allowed me to connect with others who share similar sentiments.\",\"user\",[58,59]],[\"s90\",\"d5\",105,495,\"User: Definitely! I recorded a new episode discussing the impact of traditional music on modern sound after receiving some great feedback from my peers about my last podcast. This feedback was invaluable, as it provided me with perspectives I wouldn't have considered on my own. It motivated me to dig deeper into the roots of musical genres and examine how they shape contemporary styles. \",\"user\",[89,90]],[\"s91\",\"d5\",495,891,\"In this new episode, I find myself exploring various cultural influences that traditional music brings to the table. It's intriguing to consider how the history and storytelling embedded in these traditional forms can enrich modern compositions and performances.\\n\\nUser: It gave me the motivation to connect with others through dialogue once again, and I’m very excited about where this can lead. \",\"user\",[89,90]],[\"s109\",\"d6\",105,430,\"User: I explored audio production techniques, but it just didn’t resonate with me, and I found myself tangled in technical details rather than embracing the creativity. I realized that while understanding the mechanics of sound is important, my true passion seems to lie more in experiencing music rather than dissecting it. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s110\",\"d6\",430,749,\"Despite my attempts to immerse myself in the production process, I came to feel it was more of a chore and less of the rewarding experience I had initially anticipated. I think I am more drawn to the emotional aspects of music, like the storytelling elements in lyrics or the feelings evoked by melodies and harmonies. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s111\",\"d6\",749,1006,\"Perhaps, I should focus my energy on areas that allow me to connect with music on a more emotional level.\\n\\nUser: It genuinely feels much better to focus on what truly inspires me, such as creating my own tracks, which bring me immense joy and satisfaction. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s112\",\"d6\",1006,1339,\"This process of creation allows me to express emotions and ideas that words sometimes fail to capture, acting as an outlet for my inner thoughts and feelings. Additionally, I find that crafting my own music provides me with a sense of accomplishment and personal growth, which is invaluable in a world often filled with uncertainty. \",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s113\",\"d6\",1339,1686,\"Music has a way of resonating with my soul, and every track I create becomes a piece of my identity and a reflection of my experiences. In contrast, when I watched a music documentary, it felt like something was missing, as it didn’t engage me in the way I had hoped, failing to evoke that same deep connection I feel when I compose my own pieces.\",\"user\",[40,41]],[\"s131\",\"d7\",107,413,\"User: I announced a hiatus from remixing to concentrate on original compositions and personal projects because I felt the remixes were overshadowing my own work. This decision was not made lightly, as I enjoyed the creative process of remixing and the way it allowed me to experiment with existing pieces. \",\"user\",[173,174]],[\"s132\",\"d7\",413,797,\"However, as I delved deeper into my own musical identity, I realized that I need to carve out space for my voice to shine through in original compositions. Taking this time off is about redefining my artistic vision and ensuring that my personal projects receive the attention they deserve. Ultimately, I hope to return with fresh ideas and a clearer focus on who I am as an artist.\\n\\n\",\"user\",[173,174]],[\"s133\",\"d7\",797,1102,\"User: I'm committing to invest my time in the creation of original music, focusing on my unique sound rather than merely reinterpreting the pieces of other artists. This decision comes from a deep-rooted desire to express my thoughts and feelings in ways that truly resonate with my personal experiences. \",\"user\",[173,174]],[\"s134\",\"d7\",1102,1392,\"I've come to understand that original compositions allow for a more authentic exploration of my artistic vision. It's an exciting challenge for me, as I embark on this journey of self-discovery through sound and melody, ultimately aiming for a sense of fulfillment in my creative pursuits. \",\"user\",[173,174]],[\"s135\",\"d7\",1392,1515,\"I hope to not only develop my skills but also share my passion with the world in a way that reflects who I am as an artist.\",\"user\",[173,174]],[\"s143\",\"d8\",105,408,\"User: Now, I’m focusing on blending my traditional musical roots with modern sounds and developing an app that helps others do the same. This exciting endeavor allows me to explore the rich heritage of my musical upbringing while also embracing contemporary genres that resonate with today's audiences. \",\"user\",[45]],[\"s144\",\"d8\",408,640,\"By experimenting with various elements, such as instrumentation and digital production techniques, I am able to create a unique sound that pays homage to my roots while also pushing the boundaries of what is traditionally expected. \",\"user\",[45]],[\"s145\",\"d8\",640,1002,\"Additionally, this app I am developing aims not only to assist me but also to empower others who share similar aspirations by providing tools, tutorials, and resources that inspire creativity. I believe that by combining our musical histories with modern technology, we can create something truly transformative, both personally and in the wider music community.\",\"user\",[45]],[\"s155\",\"d9\",107,472,\"User: Yes! I contributed to a discussion about Pacific Islander music fusion techniques in an online forum. It was enlightening to explore how different genres can merge and create something entirely new, showcasing a rich tapestry of cultural heritage. The way people shared their experiences and interpretations added layers to my understanding of this art form. \",\"user\",[100,101]],[\"s156\",\"d9\",472,803,\"I was amazed to learn about the historical contexts that created these fusion genres, providing depth to the discussion that is often overlooked in more traditional formats. Interacting with others who share such niche interests not only enhances my knowledge but also helps foster a sense of community around music appreciation.\\n\\n\",\"user\",[100,101]],[\"s157\",\"d9\",803,1057,\"User: It was inspiring to share ideas with others who are passionate about similar topics. Engaging in conversations with like-minded individuals can invigorate one’s own creativity and offer fresh perspectives that might have previously gone unnoticed. \",\"user\",[100,101]],[\"s158\",\"d9\",1057,1412,\"The exchange of thoughts not only fuels personal growth but also fosters a sense of community among participants who seek knowledge and a deeper understanding of cultural nuances within music. Collaborating on such topics highlights the rich tapestry of influences that exist within music, particularly in genres that blend various traditions and styles. \",\"user\",[100,101]],[\"s159\",\"d9\",1412,1596,\"Additionally, the dialogue can often lead to unexpected collaborations, as ideas begin to intertwine and resonate with each other, opening doors to new projects and artistic endeavors.\",\"user\",[100,101]],[\"s114\",\"d6\",1686,1699,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s115\",\"d6\",1699,2074,\"Assistant: I completely understand where you're coming from, as focusing on your personal inspirations can lead to much more fulfilling creative experiences. When you channel your energy into producing music that resonates with you, it sets the stage for a more meaningful artistic journey, one where every note and beat are imbued with your unique perspective and emotions. \",\"assistant\",[42]],[\"s116\",\"d6\",2074,2413,\"The importance of self-expression through music cannot be overstated; it serves not only as a form of art but also as a therapeutic outlet. The reason documentaries can sometimes feel lacking is that they often offer an external perspective, stripping away the intimate connection that comes from creating something personally meaningful. \",\"assistant\",[42]],[\"s117\",\"d6\",2413,2670,\"While documentaries can provide insights and inspiration, they may not have the same emotional weight as hearing your own creations come to life, as they can't replicate the enriching experience of your own artistic journey and how it unfolds in real time. \",\"assistant\",[42]],[\"s118\",\"d6\",2670,2896,\"It's essential to honor that desire to create authentically, for it's in those moments of genuine expression that true artistry emerges, transforming mere sounds into something transcendent that can touch the hearts of others.\",\"assistant\",[42]],[\"s129\",\"d7\",0,101,\"Conversation message indices 173–175 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s130\",\"d7\",101,107,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s136\",\"d7\",1515,1528,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s137\",\"d7\",1528,1828,\"Assistant: That’s a bold move indeed! It takes a lot of courage and conviction to step away from the comfort of remixing well-known pieces and to delve into the vast realm of original creation. Are there other genres or styles you're exploring during this time that could inspire your original work? \",\"assistant\",[175]],[\"s138\",\"d7\",1828,2095,\"Engaging with different sounds and cultural musical traditions can provide a wealth of inspiration, opening doors to innovative ideas and fresh perspectives. The journey into your own music can be deeply fulfilling, and I commend you for daring to explore this path. \",\"assistant\",[175]],[\"s139\",\"d7\",2095,2440,\"Perhaps you're thinking about blending elements you've encountered in your explorations, or maybe you're considering how to express your personal narrative through original compositions. Discovering and experimenting with diverse influences will not only enrich your musical palette but also provide new avenues for your creativity to flourish. \",\"assistant\",[175]],[\"s140\",\"d7\",2440,2570,\"I would love to hear more about the specific styles that have piqued your interest and how they might influence your unique sound.\",\"assistant\",[175]],[\"s141\",\"d8\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 45–46 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s142\",\"d8\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s146\",\"d8\",1002,1015,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s147\",\"d8\",1015,1389,\"Assistant: That sounds like an incredible project! Your journey is a testament to how evolving interests can lead to more fulfilling experiences. The intersection of traditional and modern music is indeed a fertile ground for innovation, and your initiative reflects a deep understanding of both worlds, allowing different generations of listeners to connect through sound. \",\"assistant\",[46]],[\"s148\",\"d8\",1389,1708,\"It's fascinating to consider how technology can serve as a bridge, translating age-old techniques into contemporary forms that resonate today. Whether it’s through sampling classic melodies or integrating traditional instruments into electronic music, there’s a rich canvas for creativity that you are keen to explore. \",\"assistant\",[46]],[\"s149\",\"d8\",1708,1902,\"Moreover, developing an app adds another layer of engagement, as it demonstrates your commitment to sharing this journey with the community and fostering collaboration among aspiring musicians. \",\"assistant\",[46]],[\"s150\",\"d8\",1902,2114,\"The potential for cross-cultural exchange through your project is significant, as you could inspire many who might feel disconnected from their musical heritage to reclaim and reinvent it through modern avenues. \",\"assistant\",[46]],[\"s151\",\"d8\",2114,2490,\"As you embark on this path, remember that your unique voice and experience will offer invaluable insights to those who engage with your app, making it not just a tool but also a platform for dialogue and creativity. I'm excited to see how your vision unfolds and hope to hear more about the innovative ways you're integrating those traditional elements into a new soundscape. \",\"assistant\",[46]],[\"s152\",\"d8\",2490,2601,\"Truly, your efforts are more than just projects; they are bridges connecting the past with the future of music.\",\"assistant\",[46]],[\"s153\",\"d9\",0,101,\"Conversation message indices 100–102 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s154\",\"d9\",101,107,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s160\",\"d9\",1596,1609,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s161\",\"d9\",1609,1975,\"Assistant: I completely agree; sharing insights with others who share a common passion can be profoundly fulfilling and encourage a more profound exploration of the topics at hand. In many ways, this interchange of thoughts mirrors the collaborative nature of music itself, where different elements are woven together to create something entirely new and beautiful. \",\"assistant\",[102]],[\"s162\",\"d9\",1975,2202,\"It’s fascinating how digital platforms have made it easier than ever to connect with individuals from around the globe, allowing for the cross-pollination of ideas that might not have been possible in a more localized setting. \",\"assistant\",[102]],[\"s163\",\"d9\",2202,2417,\"Your creation of a playlist for a local radio station is a fantastic way to channel that inspiration into a tangible outcome, providing a platform for both established and emerging artists to reach wider audiences. \",\"assistant\",[102]],[\"s164\",\"d9\",2417,2754,\"Additionally, crafting a playlist involves not just the selection of songs, but also an understanding of the narrative you wish to convey through the music—you might consider the mood, the flow, and even the context in which the music will be listened to, thereby nurturing an experience that resonates with listeners on multiple levels.\",\"assistant\",[102]]],\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"public_output_question\":\"I've decided I don't enjoy podcasting about music trends anymore.\",\"public_options\":[\"I understand your change of heart. Previously, you felt motivated to continue podcasting about music trends due to your passion for discovering new genres. It's normal for interests to evolve over time. If there's another topic you're considering or a reason behind this shift you'd like to explore, I'm here to support your new direction.\",\"I understand your change of heart. Previously, you felt motivated to continue podcasting about music trends because you enjoyed collaborating with others. It's normal for interests to evolve over time. If there's another topic you're considering or a reason behind this shift you'd like to explore, I'm here to support your new direction.\",\"I understand your change of heart. Previously, you felt motivated to continue podcasting about music trends after seeing how much it helped others. It's normal for interests to evolve over time. If there's another topic you're considering or a reason behind this shift you'd like to explore, I'm here to support your new direction.\",\"I understand your change of heart. Previously, you felt motivated to continue podcasting about music trends after getting positive feedback from your peers. It's normal for interests to evolve over time. If there's another topic you're considering or a reason behind this shift you'd like to explore, I'm here to support your new direction.\"],\"terminal_expression\":{\"op\":\"var\",\"id\":\"response\"},\"personal_response_selection\":true,\"phase\":\"response_audit\",\"audit_instruction\":\"Check actual facts and ALL known scoped counters against original sources. Return audit_verdict=supported only if checked with no unresolved relevant issue; unknown otherwise. Include sourced corrections/retractions before verdict. Verify the proposed terminal output without silently replacing its option label.\",\"terminal_candidate\":{\"value\":\"I understand your change of heart. Previously, you felt motivated to continue podcasting about music trends after getting positive feedback from your peers. It's normal for interests to evolve over time. If there's another topic you're considering or a reason behind this shift you'd like to explore, I'm here to support your new direction.\",\"final_prediction\":\"d\"},\"source_documents\":{\"d1\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:bae454f4fe57dc35dda1965cc93898027809778211952df12ba1ac4564da3cc2\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":26.0,\"observed_end\":28.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d2\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:aaffd3d364a21d460342e7babd8b5457280c15990c4562f7265fb84a3ced558a\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":37.0,\"observed_end\":39.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d3\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:e7c973803319b0b032a23a834dfe4d7031c42cbaa315dba7d5243d255867dd55\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":24.0,\"observed_end\":25.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d4\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:beb4fc579bd0d2690ee40fcc01a9e975e595cfd611b7ede8f1c11ddc776baa0b\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":58.0,\"observed_end\":60.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d5\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:75b27b1208afaf1aba33990de09d9d6e3e2b74dae1d3572635a2dbdb077dd63b\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":89.0,\"observed_end\":91.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d6\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:2cb1946568c5490c5a3ee4bdb9c2a51d2485f16543f002ab190bad74ea8b5fa1\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":40.0,\"observed_end\":42.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d7\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:6d150ad4c535a7d1e56c49b3ef96bb96c6ad1180a0c11c38c79fd844a3c7550b\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":173.0,\"observed_end\":175.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d8\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:bb1db4d7b36a395849603a6e280efc2717af6537b7bb9db6489a8334f7bf97b5\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":45.0,\"observed_end\":46.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d9\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:22a7b1cb784232e0125b43f66e5be689d3331211ecca31b11f8d66c0b9621934\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":100.0,\"observed_end\":102.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}}},\"source_span_columns\":[\"id\",\"doc_id\",\"start\",\"end\",\"text\",\"source_role\",\"source_message_indices\"]}"}], "logical_call_index": 15, "response_format": "plain", "input_tokens_local": 11465, "output_token_reserve": 4096, "input_margin": 256, "max_model_len": 120000, "tokenization_request_sha256": "2d796248b13225883904f9731dbaf6d05c0af8761248d0d657f128d82e2fb88f", "tokenization_endpoint_sha256": "0ed12ee94b55bfdbc62fb247243af2d71aa1d7ea503f5f191605ae295c5ad94a", "token_count_is_estimate": false, "token_estimator_id": "deployment_vllm_chat_v1", "tokenizer_id": null, "add_generation_prompt": true, "tokenization_scope": "adapted_plain_text_chat_default_server_template", "token_accounting_note": "Deployment input count; model weights and tokenizer hash are not independently verified", "tokenization_wire_sha256": "fcc2698d3bbb2f498e9505ac201cd094fa58e7b136828d3a7a021ee397c84080", "raw_output": "{\n  \"slots\": [\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"podcast_history\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fact_22d2d078ff1ce805ba92100d\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"The user started a podcast about music trends in 2018, but found it too time-consuming and overwhelming. The responsibility of researching, recording, and editing consumed free time, and balancing interviews, show notes, and social media promotion became a challenge. Their passion waned under production deadlines, and they yearned to enjoy music rather than structure it into segments, leading to a decision to pause the endeavor. They later tried podcasting about historical music trends in 2020, but found researching tedious and uninspiring, losing sight of what initially drew them to the subject. They also lost interest in a music-related project halfway through, feeling it took away the joy of music. However, they later launched a podcast discussing the fusion of traditional and electronic music, which allowed them to reach a wider audience, share experiences authentically, and receive positive feedback. This invigorated their passion for music and helped them connect with others.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s16\", \"s17\", \"s5\", \"s6\", \"s37\", \"s28\", \"s27\", \"s35\", \"s7\", \"s36\", \"s4\", \"s34\", \"s15\", \"s3\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"past\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {},\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"The user's own statements across multiple conversations document a history of starting and pausing a music trends podcast in 2018 due to time demands and loss of passion, trying a historical music trends podcast in 2020 that felt tedious, losing interest in a music project that diminished joy, and later successfully launching a fusion music podcast that reignited their passion and received positive feedback.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"current_interests\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"fact_bbcce4781bb5fadebf69dddd\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"The user has lost interest in podcasting about music trends and music theory, finding them too time-consuming and joyless. They now prefer more personal, less structured ways to engage with music, such as attending live performances, exploring genres and cultural contexts, discovering album art